    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "Seems like we have an issue with either cuSOLVER or the way we dispatch to it:\n\n```\nIn [4]: torch.linalg.lu(A)\nOut[4]: \ntorch.return_types.linalg_lu(\nP=tensor([[0., 0., 1.],\n        [0., 1., 0.],\n        [1., 0., 0.]]),\nL=tensor([[ 1.0000,  0.0000,  0.0000],\n        [    nan,  1.0000,  0.0000],\n        [-0.1429,     nan,  1.0000]]),\nU=tensor([[ 7.,  8., 10.],\n        [ 0., nan, nan],\n        [ 0.,  0., nan]]))\n\nIn [5]: torch.linalg.lu(A.cuda())\nOut[5]: \ntorch.return_types.linalg_lu(\nP=tensor([[0., 0., 1.],\n        [0., 1., 0.],\n        [1., 0., 0.]], device='cuda:0'),\nL=tensor([[ 1.0000,  0.0000,  0.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  1.0000,  0.0000],\n        [-0.1429,  0.6286,  1.0000]], device='cuda:0'),\nU=tensor([[ 7.0000,  8.0000, 10.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  5.0000,  6.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  0.0000,  0.6571]], device='cuda:0'))\n\nIn [6]: torch.backends.cuda.preferred_linalg_library(\"cusolver\")\n[W128 16:15:39.207964503 Context.cpp:444] Warning: torch.backends.cuda.preferred_linalg_library is an experimental feature. If you see any error or unexpected behavior when this flag is set please file an issue on GitHub. (function operator())\nOut[6]: <_LinalgBackend.Cusolver: 1>\n\nIn [7]: torch.linalg.lu(A.cuda())\nOut[7]: \ntorch.return_types.linalg_lu(\nP=tensor([[0., 0., 1.],\n        [0., 1., 0.],\n        [1., 0., 0.]], device='cuda:0'),\nL=tensor([[ 1.0000,  0.0000,  0.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  1.0000,  0.0000],\n        [-0.1429,  0.6286,  1.0000]], device='cuda:0'),\nU=tensor([[ 7.0000,  8.0000, 10.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  5.0000,  6.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  0.0000,  0.6571]], device='cuda:0'))\n\n...\nIn [10]: A\nOut[10]: \ntensor([[-1.,  2.,  3.],\n        [nan,  5.,  6.],\n        [ 7.,  8., 10.]])\n\nIn [11]: P @ L @ U\nOut[11]: \ntensor([[-1.0000,  2.0000,  3.0000],\n        [ 0.0000,  5.0000,  6.0000],\n        [ 7.0000,  8.0000, 10.0000]], device='cuda:0')\n```\n\nSo, it seems, `NaN`s are treated as zeroes.\n\nMAMGA is consistent with LAPACK (and, maybe, it just dispatches there).\n\n\nCC @ptrblck , @eqy ",
